Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 57/59] http client: fallback clients, through which a remote
 rule-set repeats a failed download

An HTTP client may name other shared clients as its fallbacks; a remote rule-set whose download
through its client fails or stalls repeats it through each fallback client in turn.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  eb3fdb31c http client: fallback clients, through which a remote rule-set repeats a failed download

